    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0906" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the British Secretary
                        of State for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Eden</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">and
                        Reply</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d488-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-05">December 5 (?), 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anthony</hi>
                    Has he<anchor n="2" xml:id="d488-f2"/> been told squadrons do not go in until
                    Feb 15? Is there good reason not to tell him</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Harry</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Yes; he has been told. Winston gave
                        him a paper this afternoon.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d488-f3"/> He understands,
                        but issue is he won’t agree to flying in until his <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >army</hi> is ready. This looks like a long job.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d488-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d488-f1-content">
                <p>This exchange of handwritten notes presumably occurred during the quadripartite
                    dinner meeting of December 5, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg733">p. 733</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d488-f2" n="2" xml:id="d488-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably Inönü.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d488-f3" n="3" xml:id="d488-f3-content">
                <p>The paper under reference was presumably the “plan” mentioned in the tripartite
                    meeting that afternoon; see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg714">p. 714</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
